WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.520
In good conditions, some bacteria
can divide every 20 to 30 minutes.

2
00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:08.400
Many grow on cheap nutrients, even waste,

3
00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:10.180
and need little land.

4
00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:13.530
Grow them in a fermenter, and
you have huge numbers of cells,

5
00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:15.510
all at work at once.

6
00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:19.140
So how can a tank of tiny
living cells make medicines,

7
00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:22.230
cheese, and even clean up oil spills?

8
00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:27.040
In this mission, you'll find out what
makes microorganisms such useful workers,

9
00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:29.760
from their speed to their simple needs.

10
00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:34.180
Then you'll follow them into real jobs,
from cheese-making to medicine for people

11
00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:35.740
with diabetes.

12
00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:41.200
Your mission: explain how tanks of tiny
living cells can make medicines and cheese,

13
00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:42.920
and clean up oil spills.
